# Runner images for `act` (https://nektosact.com), which runs this repo's own
# .github/workflows/ci.yml locally in Docker.
#
# Pinned here for two reasons. act prompts for an image on first run and dies
# with `level=fatal msg=EOF` under any non-interactive invocation, so without
# this a new clone cannot run act from a script. And the choice matters: the
# "large" image is a ~53 GB runner snapshot published for amd64 only, which on
# an arm64 machine means every job runs under qemu.
#
# catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest is multi-arch (amd64, arm64), ~500 MB, and
# carries enough to bootstrap the actions themselves -- which then install the
# real toolchains, exactly as they do on GitHub. That is the whole point: the
# toolchain comes from `actions/setup-go@v5`, not from an image someone has to
# remember to update.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P ubuntu-22.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04
-P ubuntu-24.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04
